# Case: Physical paste into a real target application
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Prove actual cross-application insertion independently from clipboard application.
# Steps:
#   Apply a synthetic history item through physical Enter; start an isolated GNOME Text Editor; paste, read inserted text and save through physical guest keys.
# Expected:
#   The owned editor has OS focus, its accessible text matches exactly, and its saved document matches the fixture including GtkSourceView's default trailing newline.
# Forbidden:
#   Host clipboard access, personal editor state, keys sent without verified focus, or treating dispatch alone as insertion.

start
submit target 'UNIC-D native target 中文'
ui-wait listItem 'UNIC-D native target 中文'
ui-click listItem 'UNIC-D native target 中文'
system-key Enter
system-board-equals 'UNIC-D native target 中文'
screenshot applied-before-target
system-paste-target 'UNIC-D native target 中文' expected-target.txt

-- expected-target.txt --
UNIC-D native target 中文
